<body>

<h1>CSV Data Adaptation to Web Application</h1>

<p>This document explains how data from the CSV file is loaded, transformed, and used in the Libraries Boosting Connectivity web application.</p>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">📁</span> CSV File Location</h2>

<p>The CSV file must be located at:</p>
<pre>frontend/public/arxiu_sortida.csv</pre>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">🔄</span> How Data is Loaded</h2>

<h3>Loading Process (MapPage.jsx)</h3>

<pre>
// Location: useEffect in MapPage.jsx
const res = await fetch("/arxiu_sortida.csv");
const text = await res.text();
const parsed = Papa.parse(text, {
  header: true,
  skipEmptyLines: true,
  dynamicTyping: true,
  transformHeader: (h) => String(h || "").replace(/\u00A0/g, " ").trim(),
});
</pre>

<p><strong>Features:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Uses the <strong>PapaParse</strong> library for CSV parsing</li>
<li>Headers are normalized (non-breaking spaces converted)</li>
<li>Dynamic typing enabled for automatic number conversion</li>
<li>Data is transformed to <strong>GeoJSON FeatureCollection</strong> format</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">📊</span> CSV Columns and Their Usage</h2>

<h3>Essential Columns (Required)</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>lat</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Latitude coordinate for map marker</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>lon</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Longitude coordinate for map marker</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>country</code> / <code>Country</code> / <code>COUNTRY</code> / <code>admin</code> / <code>ADMIN</code> / <code>nation</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Library country (for filtering and statistics)</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Library Name Columns</h3>

<p>The code searches for the name in this priority order:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>name</code></li>
<li><code>Name</code></li>
<li><code>Library name</code></li>
<li><code>Library Name</code></li>
<li><code>Name of library</code></li>
</ul>

<h3>Library Type Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Select the library type</code></td><td>Library type (Public, Academic, etc.)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Other (specify):Select the library type</code></td><td>Custom text if type is "Other"</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Connectivity Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Expected Values</th><th>Usage</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Does the library currently have Internet access?</code></td><td>"Yes", "No", or empty</td><td><strong>Main filter</strong>: Connected vs Not Connected</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>What type of internet connection does your library have?</code></td><td>Text (Fiber, DSL, Satellite, Cable, Mobile, etc.)</td><td>Connection type chart</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>What is the average Internet/download speed available at the library?</code></td><td>Text (see table below)</td><td>Speed halo color</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>How would you rate the current state of digital infrastructure and devices in your library?</code></td><td>Number 0-100</td><td>Perceived quality chart</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>How stable is the Internet connection?</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Displayed in library details</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Is there a separate network access for users and library staff?</code></td><td>"Yes", "No"</td><td>Displayed in details (type_connect mode)</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Reasons for No Connection Columns</h3>

<p>These columns are used when the library does NOT have internet. If they have any value (except empty, "na", "n/a", "none", "0", "false", "no"), they are counted:</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Full Column Name</th><th>Bucket</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Infrastructure limitations:Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td><code>infrastructure</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>High cost:Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td><code>high_cost</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Electrical supply issues:Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td><code>electrical</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Digital literacy gaps (library staff lacks basic digital skills so there would be underutilization of connectivity resources):Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td><code>digital_literacy</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Policy/Regulatory barriers (national regulations limit Internet access):Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td><code>policy</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>All of the above:Kindly provide a brief explanation for your previous answer below (multiple answers are possible)</code></td><td>Adds to all categories</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Basic Information Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>How many staff members work at your library (full-time equivalent)?</code></td><td>Staff count</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Date Submitted</code></td><td>Submission date (year extracted for "Data source")</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Target Audience Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Full Column Name</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Children (0-12 years):Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Teenagers (13-17 years):Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Adults (18-60 years):Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Seniors (65+ years):Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Students:Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Entrepreneurs:Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Educators / Teachers:Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Researchers / Academics:Select multiple options to specify the approximate target audience of your library</code></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Internet Access Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>How many hours per day is the Internet available to users?</code></td><td>Availability hours</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>How many computers or devices with Internet access are available for users in your library?</code></td><td>Available devices</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>More than 20 (specify):How many computers or devices with Internet access are available for users in your library?</code></td><td>Specification if &gt;20</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Please provide an approximate number for the amount of users that access the library Internet on a daily basis.</code></td><td>Daily users</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Devices Used Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Full Column Name</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Desktop computers:What devices are primarily used to access the Internet?</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Laptops:What devices are primarily used to access the Internet?</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Smartphones:What devices are primarily used to access the Internet?</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Tablets:What devices are primarily used to access the Internet?</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Other:What devices are primarily used to access the Internet?</code></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Digital Resources Columns</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>Educational websites:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Online journals:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Online courses:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>E-books:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Educational videos:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Interactive software:What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Other (specify):What types of digital resources are used at the library?</code></td><td>Resource type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Provide an approximate estimate of the number digital resources that are available in your collection</code></td><td>Resource quantity</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Are your digital resources accessible remotely? (outside of library premises)</code></td><td>Remote access</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Impact Column</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>How has the unavailability of Internet connectivity affected your library's ability to provide services to users?</code></td><td>Impact of lack of connection</td></tr>
</table>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">🔀</span> Data Transformation</h2>

<p>Each CSV row is transformed into a <strong>GeoJSON Feature</strong> with computed properties:</p>

<pre>
{
  type: "Feature",
  id: index,
  geometry: { 
    type: "Point", 
    coordinates: [lon, lat] 
  },
  properties: {
    ...allOriginalColumns,
    
    // Automatically computed properties:
    __country: "Spain",           // Normalized country
    __dlBucket: "green",          // "red" | "orange" | "green" | "unknown"
    __connBucket: "optic_fiber",  // Normalized connection type
    __reasonBucket: "high_cost",  // Reason for no connection
    __pqBucket: "good",           // Perceived quality
    hasData: true                 // Has data (name or address)
  }
}
</pre>

<h3>Download Speed Buckets (__dlBucket)</h3>

<p>Speed is calculated from the column:<br>
<code>What is the average Internet/download speed available at the library?</code></p>

<table>
<tr><th>CSV Value (contains...)</th><th>Bucket</th><th>Color</th></tr>
<tr><td>"less than 1", "between 1-5", "1-5", "less than 5"</td><td><code>red</code></td><td style="background-color:#F82055;color:white">#F82055</td></tr>
<tr><td>"between 5-20", "5-20", "between 20-40", "20-40"</td><td><code>orange</code></td><td style="background-color:#FDB900">#FDB900</td></tr>
<tr><td>"between 40-100", "40-100", "more than 100", "&gt;100"</td><td><code>green</code></td><td style="background-color:#3ED896">#3ED896</td></tr>
<tr><td>Empty or other</td><td><code>unknown</code></td><td style="background-color:#20BBCE">#20BBCE</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Connection Type Buckets (__connBucket)</h3>

<p>Connection is calculated from the column:<br>
<code>What type of internet connection does your library have?</code></p>

<table>
<tr><th>CSV Value (contains...)</th><th>Bucket</th><th>Color</th></tr>
<tr><td>"optic", "fiber", "fibre"</td><td><code>optic_fiber</code></td><td style="background-color:#FF2AAE;color:white">#FF2AAE</td></tr>
<tr><td>"dsl", "adsl", "vdsl"</td><td><code>dsl</code></td><td style="background-color:#FF8A00">#FF8A00</td></tr>
<tr><td>"satellite", "sat"</td><td><code>satellite</code></td><td style="background-color:#5CFF7A">#5CFF7A</td></tr>
<tr><td>"cable", "coax"</td><td><code>cable</code></td><td style="background-color:#D5E600">#D5E600</td></tr>
<tr><td>"mobile", "cell", "3g", "4g", "5g", "lte"</td><td><code>mobile_data</code></td><td style="background-color:#1E5BFF;color:white">#1E5BFF</td></tr>
<tr><td>"other"</td><td><code>other</code></td><td style="background-color:#7A1FFF;color:white">#7A1FFF</td></tr>
<tr><td>"unknown", "n/a", "na", "none", or empty</td><td><code>unknown</code></td><td style="background-color:#27C7D8">#27C7D8</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Perceived Quality Buckets (__pqBucket)</h3>

<p>Quality is calculated from the column:<br>
<code>How would you rate the current state of digital infrastructure and devices in your library?</code></p>

<table>
<tr><th>CSV Value (0-100)</th><th>Bucket</th><th>Color</th></tr>
<tr><td>0-19</td><td><code>very_poor</code></td><td style="background-color:#F82055;color:white">#F82055</td></tr>
<tr><td>20-49</td><td><code>poor</code></td><td style="background-color:#FF7A00">#FF7A00</td></tr>
<tr><td>50-59</td><td><code>fair</code></td><td style="background-color:#FFD400">#FFD400</td></tr>
<tr><td>60-79</td><td><code>good</code></td><td style="background-color:#8BE04E">#8BE04E</td></tr>
<tr><td>80-100</td><td><code>excellent</code></td><td style="background-color:#2EAD27;color:white">#2EAD27</td></tr>
<tr><td>Empty or invalid</td><td><code>unknown</code></td><td style="background-color:#20BBCE">#20BBCE</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Not Connected Reason Buckets (__reasonBucket)</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Situation</th><th>Bucket</th><th>Color</th></tr>
<tr><td>Only "Infrastructure limitations" selected</td><td><code>infrastructure</code></td><td style="background-color:#36A6D8;color:white">#36A6D8</td></tr>
<tr><td>Only "High cost" selected</td><td><code>high_cost</code></td><td style="background-color:#FF6C00">#FF6C00</td></tr>
<tr><td>Only "Electrical supply issues" selected</td><td><code>electrical</code></td><td style="background-color:#0EAD27;color:white">#0EAD27</td></tr>
<tr><td>Only "Digital literacy gaps" selected</td><td><code>digital_literacy</code></td><td style="background-color:#B3BE39">#B3BE39</td></tr>
<tr><td>Only "Policy/Regulatory barriers" selected</td><td><code>policy</code></td><td style="background-color:#9E65AC;color:white">#9E65AC</td></tr>
<tr><td>2+ reasons or "All of the above"</td><td><code>multi</code></td><td style="background-color:#D83A8F;color:white">#D83A8F</td></tr>
<tr><td>No reason or library is connected</td><td><code>unknown</code></td><td style="background-color:#20BBCE">#20BBCE</td></tr>
</table>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">📈</span> Calculated Statistics</h2>

<p>The application automatically calculates:</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Statistic</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>totalPoints</code></td><td>Total number of libraries</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>connectivityMapped</code></td><td>Libraries with connectivity info</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>downloadMeasured</code></td><td>Libraries with speed measurements</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>dlRed</code>, <code>dlOrange</code>, <code>dlGreen</code></td><td>Distribution by speed</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>internetYes</code>, <code>internetNo</code></td><td>Connected vs not connected</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>connectionTypeCounts</code></td><td>Count by connection type</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>perceivedQualityCounts</code></td><td>Count by quality level</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>notConnectReasonsCounts</code></td><td>Count by reason for no connection</td></tr>
</table>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">🗺️</span> Map Visualization Modes</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Mode</th><th>Active Filter</th><th>What It Shows</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>library_status</code></td><td>Default</td><td>Green=Connected, Red=No, Cyan=Unknown</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>type_connect</code></td><td>Connection type</td><td>Colors by type (fiber, DSL, etc.)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>not_connect</code></td><td>Not connected</td><td>Only libraries without internet, by reason</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>perceived_quality</code></td><td>Quality</td><td>Colors by quality level</td></tr>
</table>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">🔧</span> How to Add Multiple CSV Files</h2>

<p>If you want to use more than one CSV file, you need to modify <code>MapPage.jsx</code>:</p>

<h3>Option 1: Load Multiple CSVs and Combine Them</h3>

<pre>
// In MapPage.jsx, inside the data loading useEffect:

useEffect(() => {
  const loadAllCSVs = async () => {
    try {
      // List of CSV files to load
      const csvFiles = [
        "/arxiu_sortida.csv",
        "/arxiu_sortida_2.csv",
        "/arxiu_sortida_3.csv"
      ];
      
      let allFeatures = [];
      
      for (const csvFile of csvFiles) {
        const res = await fetch(csvFile);
        const text = await res.text();
        const parsed = Papa.parse(text, {
          header: true,
          skipEmptyLines: true,
          dynamicTyping: true,
          transformHeader: (h) => String(h || "").replace(/\u00A0/g, " ").trim(),
        });
        
        // Process each row as before
        const features = parsed.data
          .filter(row => {
            const lat = parseFloat(row.lat);
            const lon = parseFloat(row.lon);
            return !isNaN(lat) && !isNaN(lon);
          })
          .map((row, idx) => {
            // ... existing transformation ...
            return {
              type: "Feature",
              id: allFeatures.length + idx, // Unique global ID
              geometry: { type: "Point", coordinates: [lon, lat] },
              properties: { ...row, /* computed buckets */ }
            };
          });
        
        allFeatures = [...allFeatures, ...features];
      }
      
      const combinedGeojson = {
        type: "FeatureCollection",
        features: allFeatures
      };
      
      setFullGeojson(combinedGeojson);
      setGeojson(combinedGeojson);
      
    } catch (err) {
      console.error("Error loading CSVs:", err);
    }
  };
  
  loadAllCSVs();
}, []);
</pre>

<h3>Option 2: Dynamic CSV Selection</h3>

<pre>
// Add a state to control which CSV is displayed
const [selectedDataSource, setSelectedDataSource] = useState("arxiu_sortida.csv");

// Modify useEffect to reload when it changes
useEffect(() => {
  const loadCSV = async () => {
    const res = await fetch(`/${selectedDataSource}`);
    // ... rest of loading code ...
  };
  loadCSV();
}, [selectedDataSource]);

// Add a selector to the UI
&lt;select 
  value={selectedDataSource} 
  onChange={(e) => setSelectedDataSource(e.target.value)}
&gt;
  &lt;option value="arxiu_sortida.csv"&gt;Main Dataset&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option value="arxiu_europa.csv"&gt;Europe&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option value="arxiu_africa.csv"&gt;Africa&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;
</pre>

<h3>Requirements for New CSV Files</h3>

<ol>
<li><strong>Must have the same columns</strong> (or at least the required ones)</li>
<li><strong>Location</strong>: <code>frontend/public/</code></li>
<li><strong>Format</strong>: UTF-8, with headers in the first row</li>
<li><strong>Coordinates</strong>: Must have valid <code>lat</code> and <code>lon</code></li>
</ol>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">📝</span> Checklist for Adding a New CSV</h2>

<ul>
<li>☐ File is in <code>frontend/public/</code></li>
<li>☐ Has <code>lat</code> and <code>lon</code> columns (valid numbers)</li>
<li>☐ Has a country column (<code>country</code>, <code>Country</code>, <code>COUNTRY</code>, <code>admin</code>, etc.)</li>
<li>☐ Has a name column (<code>name</code>, <code>Name</code>, <code>Library name</code>, etc.)</li>
<li>☐ Connectivity columns follow the expected format</li>
<li>☐ File is in UTF-8 format</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2><span class="emoji">🐛</span> Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>Libraries don't appear on the map</h3>
<ul>
<li>Verify that <code>lat</code> and <code>lon</code> are valid numbers</li>
<li>Check that there are no whitespace issues in headers</li>
</ul>

<h3>Filters don't work</h3>
<ul>
<li>Make sure the column <code>Does the library currently have Internet access?</code> contains "Yes" or "No"</li>
<li>Reason columns must have some value to be counted</li>
</ul>

<h3>Statistics are incorrect</h3>
<ul>
<li>Verify that the column <code>What is the average Internet/download speed available at the library?</code> contains values like "Less than 1 Mbps", "Between 5-20 Mbps", etc.</li>
<li>The column <code>How would you rate the current state of digital infrastructure and devices in your library?</code> must be a number between 0 and 100</li>
</ul>

<hr>

